dump1090 (FlightAware branch)
============================

The package provides dump1090, the view1090 terminal client, and the
SkyAware web interface in /usr/share/dump1090/html.

RTL-SDR, recorded I/Q files and network input are supported. Other SDR
backends require libraries that are not currently packaged in AOSC OS.
An RTL-SDR receiver and a suitable antenna are needed for RF reception.

Receiver service
----------------
The optional dump1090.service uses a dynamic unprivileged account and writes
JSON data to /run/dump1090. RTL-SDR's udev rules provide USB device access.
Start it explicitly with:

    systemctl enable --now dump1090.service

Network listeners bind to 127.0.0.1 by default. Set additional arguments in
/etc/default/dump1090, using dump1090 --help as a reference. For example,
OPTIONS="--net-only" selects network input without opening an SDR device.
Use view1090 to display data from the local Beast output.

SkyAware
--------
The optional dump1090-web.service uses AOSC's lighttpd package to serve
SkyAware and live receiver JSON. lighttpd is installed as a runtime
dependency. Enable the service with:

    systemctl enable --now dump1090-web.service

This also starts dump1090.service. Configure the receiver as described
above, using OPTIONS="--net-only" when receiving data over the network.
Then open http://localhost:8080/.

The web service runs under its own dynamic unprivileged account. Its
configuration is /etc/dump1090/lighttpd.conf, independent of the main
lighttpd.service. By default it listens on 127.0.0.1:8080. Change server.bind
or server.port in that configuration to select another address or port,
then restart dump1090-web.service.

Map tiles require Internet access; local aircraft data is served locally.

Companion tools
---------------
/usr/libexec/dump1090/faup1090 is the upstream PiAware conversion helper.
/usr/libexec/dump1090/starch-benchmark can verify DSP implementations with
the -V option or benchmark them to generate optional DSP wisdom files.
The built-in DSP selection works without a generated wisdom file.

This package does not install or start PiAware and does not upload data
to FlightAware. Configure any external feeder separately if desired.
